  "explanation": [
    "For $y = \\sin(Bx)$ the period is $\\frac{2\\pi}{B}$.",
    "With $B = 2$ the period is $\\frac{2\\pi}{2} = \\pi$.",
    "A bigger $B$ squeezes the wave, so it repeats sooner, not later."
  ],
  "alternativeExplanations": [
    {
      "title": "Chase the input",
      "steps": [
        "A sine curve completes one cycle when its input runs from $0$ to $2\\pi$.",
        "The input here is $2x$, so we need $2x$ to travel from $0$ to $2\\pi$.",
        "That means $x$ only travels from $0$ to $\\pi$ — the period is $\\pi$."
      ]
    }
  ],
